From f3d7430e8d38fdeb0897c377c56f04cbaf0bb21a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: beau4201 <beau.ten.berge@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:18:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Wifi: do not derive the link-local IPv6 address from the MAC

With MAC randomisation ClientModeImpl asked for EUI-64 link-local
addresses, which embed the random MAC. LinkProperties hands that address
to every app with ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE while WifiInfo redacts the MAC, so
the address gives the MAC away. Use the default of ProvisioningConfiguration,
the stable privacy mode, which does not embed it.
---
 service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java
index 26d376950c..71a439775b 100644
--- a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java
+++ b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java
@@ -8708,10 +8708,11 @@ public class ClientModeImpl extends StateMachine implements ClientMode {
                         .withCreatorUid(config.creatorUid)
                         .withLayer2Information(layer2Info)
                         .withDhcpOptions(convertToInternalDhcpOptions(options));
-        if (isUsingMacRandomization) {
-            // Use EUI64 address generation for link-local IPv6 addresses.
-            prov.withRandomMacAddress();
-        }
+        // FreeholdOS: the link-local IPv6 address is never derived from the interface MAC. With MAC
+        // randomisation the EUI-64 form is the random MAC itself, which is stable per network, and
+        // LinkProperties hands that address to every app that holds ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE, while
+        // WifiInfo redacts the same MAC. The default of ProvisioningConfiguration is the stable
+        // privacy mode, which does not embed the MAC.
         if (mContext.getResources().getBoolean(R.bool.config_wifiEnableApfOnNonPrimarySta)
                 || isPrimary()) {
             // unclear if the native layer will return the correct non-capabilities if APF is
-- 
